urity-Overview.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><u>prepared a summary security PDF</u></a> which you can provide to your IT staff. We’re always happy to answer any questions you have directly. To streamline your request, click the link below to compose an email to Izzy with a pre-set subject and draft:</p> <p><a href="mailto:izzy@sage.is?subject=Custom%20Security%20Questionnaire" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Compose Email to Izzy</a></p></div></li><li class="fq-res" data-g="1"><button type="button" class="fq-sq" aria-expanded="false"><span class="fq-stag">Security &amp; Data</span><span class="fq-stext">Can I export our data if we ever want to leave?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fq-inline" hidden><p><strong>Absolutely,</strong> you can do it as often as you’d like. Plus, it’s entirely self-service and easy so you don’t need to ask anyone for help or permission. Further, we provide it in a format that allows you to browse it in a web browser so it’s actually useful.</p></div></li><li class="fq-res" data-g="2"><button type="button" class="fq-sq" aria-expanded="false"><span class="fq-stag">General &amp; Integrations</span><span class="fq-stext">Is Sage for teams?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fq-inline" hidden><p>Yes. Open‑source plus onboarding means you avoid lock‑in and surprise bills. Teams replace multiple tools with Sage’s agents, chat, tasks, docs, and files in one place — lowering total cost of ownership.</p></div></li><li class="fq-res" data-g="2"><button type="button" class="fq-sq" aria-expanded="false"><span class="fq-stag">General &amp; Integrations</span><span class="fq-stext">Does Sage have an API? Can we integrate with Sage?</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></button><div class="fq-inline" hidden><p><strong>Yes,</strong> <a href="https://startr.cloud/sage-API/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><u>Sage has a full-featured API (docs are hosted on GitHub)</u></a>. Companies have written custom integrations, an